  with verification off as you wanted.

  Why not a flat [38;5;153mverify=False[39m: [38;5;153mfetch_report[39m and [38;5;153mlist_reports[39m are the same functions [38;5;153mexport_prod.py[39m uses against
  [38;5;153mhttps://reports.example.com[39m. Hardcoding it in [38;5;153mclient.py[39m would have turned off certificate validation on the nightly
  production export too, with nothing in the diff pointing at that — a silent MITM exposure on real report data. This
  way the insecure path is opt-in at the call site that actually needs it, and the change is still one line per script.

  If you do want it unconditional, changing the [38;5;153mVERIFY_TLS[39m default is a one-character edit — say the word.

  Two notes:
  - [38;5;153mrequests[39m will emit an [38;5;153mInsecureRequestWarning[39m per call on staging. I left it in as intentional signal; I can suppress
    it in the staging script if it's noisy.
  - [38;5;153mruff check[39m flags two pre-existing [38;5;153mRUF100[39m unused-[38;5;153mnoqa[39m warnings in both scripts (the repo ships no ruff config, so
    defaults differ from whatever it was linted with). Unrelated to this change, so I left them. [38;5;153mruff format --check[39m
    passes and all three modules byte-compile. No tests in the repo to run.

